    ...
} else {
    NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(extack, "Eswitch vport is disabled");
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code attempts to log an error message when querying the hardware address of a disabled E-switch vport. This is unnecessary since the disabled state is expected behavior, and logging an error in this case can lead to confusion.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (vport->enabled) {
    ...
} 
// Removed else block that sets the error message
```
Reason:
The fix involves removing the else block that sets the error message for a disabled vport. By doing this, the code avoids generating an error log when the vport is disabled, thus preventing misleading error messages and aligning the behavior with the expected functionality.

